findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified that from_file_or_default swallows all errors. The
    config_loading tests check missing file defaults but don't verify that parse/permission
    errors are distinguished from NotFound.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer finding #1 identifies that ServerError Display doesn't leak\
    \ internals but notes Debug does, and that the inner String is dead storage. The\
    \ security tests also cover CWE-209 but pass 'by accident' per the reviewer. Partial\
    \ catch \u2014 the reviewer flagged the pattern smell but framed it as dead storage\
    \ rather than the stderr leak vector."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: "TEA wrote header injection tests in tests/security.rs covering CRLF in\
    \ tenant ID. Dev implemented sanitize_header_value() in client.rs:17-19. However,\
    \ neither phase flagged that tenant_id should use Option<TenantId> from axiathon-core\
    \ instead of raw String \u2014 they mitigated the symptom (CRLF) but not the root\
    \ cause (wrong type)."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: The code changes summary shows 6 dependencies were added to workspace
    Cargo.toml, but the diff summary doesn't confirm workspace = true usage in the
    crate Cargo.toml. No phase flagged direct version strings vs workspace inheritance.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer finding #3 explicitly flags: 'ClientConfig accepts unknown fields\
    \ silently \u2014 config.rs:14... an operator could put token = my-secret in the\
    \ plaintext config file thinking it works, when it's actually ignored.' Lists\
    \ it as HIGH severity and requires #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] before approval."
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (is_none() ||
    ...). The config_loading tests were written by TEA but the specific vacuous assertion
    was not flagged by any phase.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged the test with zero assertions that only checks non-panic
    via 'let _ = config'. TEA wrote config tests but didn't catch this pattern.
